From: jeffreyeffendy <jeffreyeffendy@fb.com>
Date: Sun, 29 Mar 2026 09:41:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 48/63] Re-enable Casimir NFC emulator on macOS

Summary:
Casimir was previously commented out due to an inherited_fd issue on macOS/Darwin hosts. Now that the inherited_fd issue is fixed (D98664615), Casimir can be re-enabled.

This fixes the continuous "Failed to open socket" error spam in launcher.log when the socket never existed before.

Test Plan:
```
$ . build/envsetup.sh
$ lunch aosp_cf_arm64_phone-userdebug
$ m out/host/darwin-x86/cvd-host_package.tar.gz

$ device device virtual -t <device> --cache-only
$ cd ~/.device/cache/emulators/<device>_cf_emu_arm64-15910000003901-1644523956582521
$ ln -s ~/cvd-tools/out/host/darwin-x86/cvd-host_package/* .
$ ./start_cuttlefish.py
...
VIRTUAL_DEVICE_BOOT_STARTED
VIRTUAL_DEVICE_NETWORK_ETHERNET_CONNECTED
VIRTUAL_DEVICE_BOOT_COMPLETED
Virtual device booted successfully
```
Seeing sign of casimir working in launcher log P2255088167
```
